From: Daryl Denson <9751141+denson9874@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 01:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] update_engine: verify payload and metadata signatures again

Evolution X's 59fbd47 ("update_engine: Always disable signature and
downgrade checks") makes PayloadVerifier::VerifySignature() return true
without looking at the signature. Every payload and metadata signature
check goes through it: update_engine on the phone (DeltaPerformer's
VerifyPayload and PayloadMetadata::ValidateMetadataSignature) and the
host delta_generator --public_key that check_ota_package_signature runs.
So the phone installs a payload signed with any key, or none, and the
host check reports "Payload signatures VERIFIED" for any payload.

Put back AOSP's VerifySignature() (android-17.0.0_r1, as LineageOS
lineage-24.0 has it): a payload installs only if its signatures verify
against a key in /system/etc/security/otacerts.zip, and fails with
ErrorCode::kDownloadPayloadPubKeyVerificationError (18) or
kDownloadMetadataSignatureMismatch (26) otherwise.

This is the signature half of 59fbd47; 0002 puts back the downgrade
check it also removed.
---
 payload_consumer/payload_verifier.cc |    6 ++----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/payload_consumer/payload_verifier.cc b/payload_consumer/payload_verifier.cc
index 9c135f45..83ef8c9e 100644
--- a/payload_consumer/payload_verifier.cc
+++ b/payload_consumer/payload_verifier.cc
@@ -95,9 +95,7 @@ std::unique_ptr<PayloadVerifier> PayloadVerifier::CreateInstanceFromZipPath(
 
 bool PayloadVerifier::VerifySignature(
     const string& signature_proto, const brillo::Blob& sha256_hash_data) const {
-  LOG(INFO) << "Payload signature verification skipped";
-  return true;
-  /*TEST_AND_RETURN_FALSE(!public_keys_.empty());
+  TEST_AND_RETURN_FALSE(!public_keys_.empty());
 
   Signatures signatures;
   LOG(INFO) << "signature blob size = " << signature_proto.size();
@@ -142,7 +140,7 @@ bool PayloadVerifier::VerifySignature(
   for (const auto& sig_hash_data : tested_hashes) {
     utils::HexDumpVector(sig_hash_data);
   }
-  return false;*/
+  return false;
 }
 
 bool PayloadVerifier::VerifyRawSignature(
